{"version":2,"text":"2.\n\nThe notice is giving information about\n\nA\n\nways of checking that an NG tube has been placed correctly.\n\nB\n\nhow the use of NG feeding tubes is authorised.\n\nC\n\nwhich staff should perform NG tube placement.\n\nE\nL\n\nNG feeding tubes\n\nDisplacement of nasogastric (NG) feeding tubes can have serious implications if undetected. Incorrectly\n\npositioned tubes leave patients vulnerable to the risks of regurgitation and respiratory aspiration. It is crucial to\n\ndifferentiate between gastric and respiratory placement on initial insertion to prevent potentially fatal pulmonary\n\nP\nM\n\ncomplications. Insertion and care of an NG tube should therefore only be carried out by a registered doctor or\n\nnurse who has undergone theoretical and practical training and is deemed competent or is supervised by someone\n\ncompetent. Assistant practitioners and other unregistered staff must never insert NG tubes or be involved in the\n\ninitial confirmation of safe NG tube position.\n\nA\nS\n\nSAMPLE\n\n[CANDIDATE NO.] READING QUESTION PAPER PARTS B & C 03/16\n\nPage 89","layout":{"version":1,"width":595.276001,"height":841.890015,"blocks":[{"text":"2.","lines":[{"text":"2.","x":0.10195758252985576,"y":0.08884928276527902,"width":0.014010307800061994,"height":0.016557982339296437,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"2.","x":0.10195758252985576,"width":0.014010307800061994,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"The notice is giving information about","lines":[{"text":"The notice is giving information about","x":0.1495766633467893,"y":0.08899181919861587,"width":0.27824063244908137,"height":0.015809666064278007,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"The","x":0.1495766633467893,"width":0.028944556761998527,"confidence":1},{"text":"notice","x":0.1831913227088085,"width":0.04481954581602561,"confidence":1},{"text":"is","x":0.23268097112485475,"width":0.012128827615880989,"confidence":1},{"text":"giving","x":0.24947990134075643,"width":0.04387880572393512,"confidence":1